# Orbit Omni section QA (locked forward)

**Locked** on `006_Could-Life-Exist-Under-The-Ice-Of-Europa` Parts **01–08** (broadcast `europa_broadcast_v01.mp4`, 2026-08-14). Apply to **every** Omni-forward long. Pipeline overview: `orbit-omni-longform-playbook.mdc` · `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/OMNI_LONGFORM_PLAYBOOK.md`.

## Process

1. **~1 minute parts.** Write → script QA → VO + Omni for that part only → picture QA.
2. **Ben UAT (blocking):** stop and check with Ben after each minute. Do not start the next part until he passes it (or asks for a regen).
3. **Do not** generate the full episode in one pass. Regen only the failed minute / failed plates.
4. Prefer **Omni Flash** continuous journey takes + **native SFX** under Ben Orbit Narrator VO (this episode). Keep VO-literal picture.
5. After Ben passes a part: update lessons log; stitch cumulative master when useful.

## Motion coverage (no “broken video” freezes)

1. **Never freeze-pad** (`tpad` / last-frame clone) to stretch short Omni clips to VO length — it looks broken.
2. **Never loop / slow-mo** scenery (see `orbit-cutscene-no-reuse`).
3. Size inventory so **1× motion covers VO**: plan ~**8–10 unique ~8s Omni plates per ~60–80s** (or more). If short, **generate more unique plates** — do not pad.
4. Assembler must **fail** (or trim ≤~1s of VO) rather than freeze-extend picture.
5. **Scenery-only quota (25 Aug 2026):** of those plates, **≥2 per minute with no Orbit at all** (pure scenery — the object VO names). They cut fine in the film and they are the only native source of scene-first Shorts covers; Shorts cut from all-Orbit minutes had no usable cover frame and needed parent-film rescues (`orbit-title-thumb-formula.mdc`).

## Character in the scene (user lock — Flow share QA)

Reference feel: Orbit flying the solar system — he **turns**, you see **exhaust / propulsion**, he **flies off**, with **native SFX**. Reads as a character *in* the world, not a sticker on wallpaper.

1. **Orbit interacts with the scene** — bank/turn, push off, skim, tip, dive, react to ice/pull/heat. Body language + motion sell presence.
2. **Readable agency:** soft underside glow as he moves; tiny bubble wake underwater OK. **Propulsion lock:** exactly **ONE** centered **bottom** underside glow — gyroscope / hover-pad style (same as space). Forbidden: twin thrusters, left+right jets, rear+bottom dual exhaust, side engines, mid-part switch to underwater **flames / fire plumes**.
3. **Camera treats him as subject in space** — parallax past ice/planets, approaching or leaving frame with intent — not locked dead-center hover for the whole take.
4. Prompts should include a concrete verb of interaction (turns toward, skims along, plunges through, banks past) + continuous motion + native whoosh/rumble SFX.
5. Reject plates where Orbit is a static ornament floating in pretty scenery while the world does all the work.
6. Travel beats: prefer gaze / nose along **direction of travel** (not always staring at camera).
7. **Neutron Star Part 01 UAT (locked forward):** do not park Orbit static in one place looking around for the whole take. Prefer bank / skim / tumble / stretch / push-off. A hang beat may hold station only when the VO is “hangs in the dark,” and then he is a **tiny figure in the void**, not a foreground hero.

## Picture quality bar (Parts 01–02 lock)

1. **VO-literal journey** — Orbit doing the line (skim cracks while VO says scars; dive when VO goes under the ice). When VO names an object, **cut to that object** (Neutron Star Part 02 teaspoon vs mountains — gold beat to copy).
2. **Gold beat to keep:** Orbit low over Europa linea + native Omni SFX while VO names cracks/scars. **Neutron Star:** metal teaspoon vs mountains while VO says a teaspoon outweighs mountains.
3. **Europa surface:** pale cream-white ice + fine dark linea. Avoid large brown/red circular “pools” unless the beat is intentionally melt/chaos.
4. When VO enters the ocean / under the lid: **lean into the dive** (crack → plunge → subsurface ocean) — intentional water OK; muddy surface pools not.
5. **Style:** premium **CGI 3D polish** (realistic materials/lighting). Reject 2D cartoon outlines / flat cel-shade when it breaks continuity with approved plates.
6. **Env honesty:** underwater plates stay submerged under ice; vacuum/space/above-ice plates stay dry. Never ship space/surface with underwater bubble trails.
7. Tag plates `env: underwater | surface | space` and **gate water SFX** to underwater windows only.

## Single Orbit / single face (hard)

1. **Exactly one Orbit** in frame at all times. Twin / clone / reflection duplicate / ghost double-exposure = reject and regen.
2. **Exactly one face** — one front black visor with cream eyes + pupils. Reject clear second rear/side faceplate or mirrored eyes on the back (Europa Part 02 · Neutron Star Part 01).
3. **Turns:** if Orbit rotates away from camera, we see the **solid matte orange back** (antenna stem + a small hatch OK). A second visor or pair of eyes appearing mid-turn is the same reject as twins.
4. Spot-check frames across each new plate (start / mid / end) before locking the rough.
5. Do **not** I2V wide/acting plates from the full-frame identity still — it parks Orbit as a foreground hero and often stamps a visor on every side. Attach a start frame that already has the correct scale, camera, and (for back shots) no visor.
6. Eyes: cream/white **with dark pupils** — never blank solid white ovals.
7. **On-model or regen.** Knockoff (no visor, no arms, glowing belly, slit LEDs) is a different character. Attach the canonical identity still plus a composition start frame — do not I2V a muddy tiny crop and hope.

## Clean vacuum (Neutron Star Part 01 UAT)

1. Space plates: **near-black**, a handful of faint pinpricks at most, **one** main distant star when the line needs it.
2. Reject dense star-noise / tiled white specks covering the black. The void should feel clear, not grainy.

## Shot grammar (no formula approach — Neutron Star Part 01–02 UAT, locked forward)

The default Omni template is **Orbit in a corner + destination opposite + look/fly toward it**. That is not a film. Reject it when it repeats.

**Neutron Star Part 02 PASS (Ben 17 Aug 2026):** too many plates were Orbit + a distant remnant — pretty pictures under clever VO. Sound and character stay. Picture must **tell the story**. Mute the VO: you should still follow the beat. Each ~1-min part, when stitched, has to play as one episode of a series (character living the universe’s story), not B-roll with a podcast on top. **Gold beat:** teaspoon vs mountains — when VO names an object, cut to that object in the same clear format.

1. **One VO idea → one literal image.** If VO and picture disagree, picture is wrong. Stretch when VO says tear into a line; a ring of *light* when VO says light bends into a ring; a living giant star when VO says it began as a giant; a **metal teaspoon vs mountains** when VO says teaspoon; kitchen lead/osmium when VO is on Earth density — not another remnant portrait.
2. **Forbidden formula:** Orbit parked in any corner, destination on the other side, then travel toward it. Do not use this as the default plate.
3. **Cap:** at most **one** Orbit + distant-remnant establishing plate per minute. The rest must be the thing the line names (object, body, interior, cutaway, visor, act).
4. **Subject follows the line.** If the line is about the star dying, the star is the subject. If it is about seeing/feeling, a visor CU is allowed. Scenery-only plates are allowed when Orbit is not who the line is about. If the line is “you are the object approaching,” the camera treats Orbit as the incoming mass — not a tourist looking at a dot.
5. Vary camera per plate: EWS hang · subject-is-the-star · weightless tumble with no destination · tidal stretch · ring-fills-frame · visor CU · living-star · supernova wall · remnant macro · Earth cutaway · interior physics. Do not rhyme two plates in a row.
6. **Mute test before gen.** If the plate would still make sense swapped with the previous Orbit+star hang, rewrite it.

## Omni SFX joins

1. Hard concat of Omni beds makes the soundtrack **stop/jump** at every cut — feels like a break.
2. Assemble with **paired `xfade` + `acrossfade`** (~0.35–0.45s) so picture and Omni SFX blend across plate joins while staying A/V locked.
3. Keep Omni SFX under VO (typical ~0.18–0.2 volume); do not strip native beds unless QA asks.
4. **Score vs Omni beds:** each Omni plate brings its own ~8s native bed. Hard concat (and even a short acrossfade) reads as music restarting at every cut. Mix a **single continuous underscore** under VO for the minute; duck it under narration; keep Omni SFX as quiet texture only. Do not treat plate beds as the score.
5. Under-ice minutes: light continuous water-movement / bubble bed under Omni SFX — **only while picture is underwater**.

## Prompt / gen hygiene

1. Prompts: continuous motion the whole clip; target ~8–10s; no freeze; single Orbit; single face; VO-literal verb; **character-in-scene interaction**; **premium CGI**; env lock (underwater vs vacuum) + bubble rules matching env.
2. Run Flow Omni gens in a **durable foreground** session; skip-existing + per-plate retry; reject ultra-fast suspect downloads when possible.
3. Archive rejected plates (`_rejected_*`); bump asset version (`v02`/`v03`) rather than overwriting without a trail.

